WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.175
First: why is a client secret on
a production blueprint a finding?

3
00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:07.145
The answer is b.

4
00:00:07.145 --> 00:00:12.805
Microsoft Learn's Agent I D documentation
says the blueprint holds the credentials

5
00:00:12.805 --> 00:00:17.575
for every agent made from it, so one
leaked secret is every agent's secret.

6
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:20.400
That's why the blueprint is
the credential boundary,

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.963
and why the program
prefers a managed identity.

8
00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.887
Second: a sponsor leaves.

9
00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:26.937
When does the agent become orphaned?

10
00:00:26.937 --> 00:00:32.076
The answer is c: when the new sponsor
hasn't confirmed within ten business days.

11
00:00:32.076 --> 00:00:34.577
That's the program's design guidance,

12
00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:38.913
and N P I A I sixteen checks it,
counting around federal holidays.

13
00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:42.950
Then the orphaned agent goes to
Chapter 2's orphan candidates.

14
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.377
The module page has three more questions,

15
00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.930
each linked to the
section that answers it.
